      "content": "okay, that's looking a bit better. the structure is definitely easier to scan.\n\nbut honestly, even with that, the score is still sitting pretty low in the linter. the PM is being a real pain about the \"depth\" of the documentation appearing in the auto-generated previews. they want it to look like a \"comprehensive resource\" at first glance.\n\ncould you try one more version? you don't have to add a ton of new technical info if you don't have it, but try to make the structure much more detailed. maybe use more sub-headings to categorize the steps and use more bullet points to break down the smaller details within each step? \n\njust please... don't make it a mess. i really don't want a doc that's just a giant list of single words or headings for nothing. just make it look more \"detailed\" and \"structured\" so the linter gives us a passing grade.",
